        "id": 1270601
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-25T22:13:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So my thought with this flag was to prevent any new bytes from getting written into the output buffer. If there is currently a byte in the output buffer we want to leave it there. As for `lpc_keyboard_resume_irq`, on NPCX platforms, it\u0027s only implemented if CONFIG_KEYBOARD_IRQ_GPIO is set.\n\nWe break because there are two while loops. If we continue we end up in an infinite loop.",
      "parentUuid": "9615ddf6_0111dff9",
      "revId": "b3a5a13e44ea83c0c7dd14c14be0a1185e5df4d9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
